		{
			dependencies: ["3EDF27DDA2C82676"]
			description: [
				"With Batteries, you can replace the remaining tools that do not have a machine equivalent with tools that can be used in world. Drills are the most immediately useful, as the LV one has the same capabilities as your Mining Hammers while having more durability, and the ones from later tools have an even &olarger&r mining area, scaling up to 9x9x9 with the IV drill. There are other power tools, including a Wrench, Wire Cutter, Screwdriver, and more. "
				"These all have an energy capacity equal to the battery used in the battery pack, and they have an unbreaking-like effect when filled with energy, where the durability itself only goes down at random. When the energy runs out, it uses durability like normal. Breaking a power tool returns you the battery pack, so you only need to bolt on another tool head."
			]
			id: "5EF0D11E54B96EAE"
			tasks: [{
				id: "4FD07F509A50D44D"
				item: {
					Count: 1
					id: "ftbfiltersystem:smart_filter"
					tag: {
						"ftbfiltersystem:filter": "ftbfiltersystem:item_tag(forge:tools/drills)"
					}
				}
				title: "Any #forge:tools/drills"
				type: "item"
			}]
			title: "Power Tools"
			x: -4.0d
			y: 2.5d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["3EDF27DDA2C82676"]
			description: ["You now have access to an Item Magnet, which makes in world item drops a nonissue. You have a dedicated Curios slot for this as well."]
