		}
		{
			dependencies: ["4798AEB718C0948B"]
			description: [
				"It's time to dive into some ore processing!"
				"Diodes are the primary novel component of Good Electronic Circuits, which are your first MV circuits. "
				"There are multiple recipes for these, but the only one you can make currently is the least efficient one, using Copper Fine Wire, Liquid Glass, and Gallium Arsenide Dust. The first two should be simple enough, but Gallium Arsenide is a bit more involved."
				""
				"You need to obtain Gallium and Arsenic. Gallium can be obtained by processing Sphalerite in a few different ways. You can electrolyze Sphalerite Dust for a small chance at getting Gallium, but try to find a better way to process it!"
				"Arsenic is much simpler, you only need to locate Realgar and electrolyze it in dust form. "
				""
				"Note that Arsenic is the first material that you will obtain that has a hazardous property, causing Arsenicosis through inhalation. This is a fancy way of saying, do not have it in your inventory for an extended period of time. The grace period is very lenient, but if you keep it on your person for too long, you eventually get a Hunger status effect, continuing to hold it will inflict Wither, almost certainly killing you."
				"You can also avoid the problem entirely by only handling Arsenic through automation, but again, the grace period is very forgiving."
			]
			id: "68993A775ACA091B"
			tasks: [{
				id: "5B8B8F62F26B97A9"
				item: "gtceu:diode"
				type: "item"
			}]
			x: 0.0d
			y: 6.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["4798AEB718C0948B"]
			description: [
				"The next tier of circuit board, this one is the first that reflects the process to create most others for the rest of the game."
				"To make the base boards, you can simply do Wood Pulp and Glue in an assembler, but you have a choice to make involving finishing the full circuit board."
				"The first option is the crafting grid recipe of surrounding the board in silver wire. This is more resource intensive but substantially easier in the short term."
				"The second option is to engage in some chemistry and create Iron III Chloride or Sodium Persulfate and mix that with the board and silver foil. Once you create a setup for those chemicals, the overall resource cost is much easier."
				"Starting at the next tier of circuit board, the chemistry route is the only one available, and it uses the same process, so it may be in your best interest to bite the bullet on the more complex route now to futureproof your factory. You'll find that decisions like these will not stop showing up."
			]
			id: "04DE51E233CBE644"
			subtitle: "Phenol not included"
			tasks: [{
				id: "2341E5F83B6D81DE"
				item: "gtceu:phenolic_printed_circuit_board"
				type: "item"
			}]
			x: 1.0d
			y: 6.0d
		}
